  "notes": "⛔ **Drum-forward by documented division of labour**: he supplies drums and structure, Soopafly supplies keys and bass, so this model is authored as a kit with harmony added second — the busiest kick in the LA group (`densityPerBar` [4,6] on 1, the and-of-2 and 3), a snare doubled with a clap, and 16th hats. It is deliberately the *complement* of the Soopafly entry, which carries the same sessions from the keyboard side: Daz's chords are a plain 2-bar `i–VI–VII` at high triad weight, Soopafly's are minor 7th/9th cycles. The one arrangement fact that is modellable is the bass shape the research names — \"running 8th-note lines under verses collapsing to sustained roots under hooks\" — authored as `independent_riff` with continuous motion and a mid `followRootsProb` so the line can do both. \"32nd rolls into section changes\" is exactly this batch's fill fingerprint, which is a coincidence worth stating rather than a claim the fingerprint was derived from him. ⚠ `medium` on the research's high-medium. INFERRED: every velocity and density number; documented are the kick placement, the doubled snare/clap, the 16th hats, the `i–VI–VII` family and the 2-bar loop.",
